sghtmltopdf is an HTML-to-PDF renderer in the spirit of wkhtmltopdf,
written in Rust and without requiring a browser engine. It builds the
layout engine itself, using html5ever for HTML parsing, and the Servo
cssparser and selectors crates for CSS parsing and matching.

It targets documents that flow top to bottom with explicit page breaks
(invoices, receipts, reports) rather than arbitrary web pages. Page
breaks, CSS fragmenting, and @page margin boxes are first-class, and pages
stream out as soon as their layout is final, so memory does not grow with
document size.

The CLI can render a file, or run an HTTP server that returns PDF for posted
HTML.
